From e2e40c76f172f17403a9d1138d9e1da21cb99986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 04:04:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(spec decode): honor DSpark anchor sampling layout

vLLM 0.26.0's Speculators converter unconditionally selects the bonus-anchor
layout. For checkpoints with sample_from_anchor=true, including
skt/A.X-K2-DSpark, the anchor predicts the first draft token and the existing
runtime expects N query slots rather than 1+N. Honor the checkpoint setting
to avoid that layout mismatch. False or absent retains the existing layout.

This configuration fix applies to any DSpark checkpoint using this converter.
Current upstream vLLM top of tree supports the same behavior by deriving
dspark_bonus_anchor from sample_from_anchor:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/995e8581f462a13e32f30cfba946c63d48cf31d7/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py

SKT already honored sample_from_anchor as part of its larger DSpark support
effort on vLLM 0.23. This local patch preserves that behavior using the DSpark
runtime already present in vLLM 0.26, without importing SKT's older runtime:
https://github.com/SKT-AI/vllm/commit/97045d9e981dbe41903938c46d1d3a00ab5c64ce

Dynamo currently applies this series only to CUDA images; CPU and XPU images
retain the upstream 0.26 behavior. The build-time validator checks the A.X-K2
DSpark configuration conversion, but non-A.X-K2 DSpark checkpoint inference
has not been validated by this port.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py b/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py
index e034cec97..90ff5271b 100644
--- a/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py
+++ b/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/speculators/algos.py
@@ -148,8 +148,13 @@ def update_dspark(config_dict: dict, pre_trained_config: dict) -> None:
         target_layer_ids (DSpark's i-1 layer semantics).
     """
     pre_trained_config["architectures"] = ["Qwen3DSparkModel"]
-    # Speculators DSpark uses the 1+N fill-in block (anchor is a bonus token).
-    pre_trained_config["dspark_bonus_anchor"] = True
+    # Preserve the block layout declared by the checkpoint. When
+    # sample_from_anchor is true, the anchor predicts the first draft token and
+    # DSpark needs N query slots. Otherwise it uses the 1+N fill-in layout where
+    # the anchor is a separate bonus token.
+    pre_trained_config["dspark_bonus_anchor"] = not config_dict.get(
+        "sample_from_anchor", False
+    )
 
     aux_layer_ids = config_dict["aux_hidden_state_layer_ids"]
     pre_trained_config["eagle_aux_hidden_state_layer_ids"] = aux_layer_ids
-- 
